* Roland TB-303 VCF, from the service notes (First Edition, 1982, p. 5, and p. 8's Fig. 2; D275): the diode ladder,
* its drive and read-out, the resonance's feedback, the exponential converter and the knobs' network. The reference
* for CoolSynth 303's filter.
*
* Rails as ideal sources: 12 V, 5.333 V; the filter's own rail through R95 (100 ohm) and C28 (47 uF).
* Transistors: the 2SC945(P) and 2SA733(P) as vco.cir has them (Fairchild's 2N3904 and 2N3906, IS from the parts'
* typical VBE: Q11's current against Q10's sets the cutoff, so their ratio matters); the duals Q12 and Q21
* (2SC1583) and Q22 (2SC2291) as matched NPNs of hFE 500 (no published models). Q13 to Q17 and Q23 are 2SC945s
* wired as diodes.
*
* The ladder: Q12's collectors pull its two sides down through four rungs of diodes (Q13, Q14, Q16 left; Q15, Q17,
* Q23 right) from Q22's emitters; C18 (0.018 uF) across the bottom rung, C19, C24, C26 (0.033 uF) above. Q21, a
* differential pair on a 0.52 mA tail (Q20), reads the top through C25 and C27 (0.1 uF); Q19 buffers it to C14.
* R110 and R111 are 22k: the service notes print 2.2k, a misprint (the x0xb0x's schematic, Open Music Labs' redraw,
* and Eddy Bergman's build have 22k); with 2.2k the resonance's loop gains about 1.3 and the filter never rings.
* The input: the waveform through R62 (220k) and C17 into Q12's left base; the feedback: the RESONANCE pot's first
* gang (VR4, 50k B) from C14's side, C15, Q18 and C23, R97 into Q12's right base.
*
* The current: Q11's collector (through R69). Q9 (2SA733) holds the converter's common node (VQ9) near 3.3 V; Q10
* (2SA733), a follower, sets Q11's base above its own (p. 8, Fig. 2). CUTOFF FREQ (VR3, 50k A) from 12 V to R47
* feeds Q10's emitter through R73 and TM3 (470k): the knob scales the current, Q10's base sets it exponentially.
* Q10's base: R71 (2.2k) to VQ9, R63 (220k) from ENV MOD's wiper (VR5, 50k A, from the envelope at its pin 3 to R61
* and VQ9 at its pin 1), R72 (100k) from the RESONANCE pot's second gang, which lies between R46 (from D24, the
* ACCENT knob's wiper) and C13 (1 uF).
*
* The audio-taper pots (A) as 15 % at half turn (R = (e^(3.47 x) - 1) / (e^3.47 - 1) of the whole from pin 1).
* TP6 is Q19's emitter (5.7 V at rest, as page 5's sketch draws it between 5.2 and 5.8 V); C14's output (nvcf) is
* loaded by VR4's first gang and the VCA's input (taken as 220k and 0.01 uF to 5.333 V, IC15's bias, until vca.cir).
*
* Parameters: cutoff, res, envmod (each the knob's turn, 0..1), env (volts at ENV MOD's top; the envelope at rest
* is near 0 V), acc (volts at D24's anode: the ACCENT knob's wiper), tm3 (0..1 of TM3's resistance), freq (the input
* saw's frequency, Hz; 0 for none), sq (1: the input is a square from 5.333 to 8.8 V instead), tend. tm3 as calibrate.py sets it by
* page 7: a 2.000 ms ring at TP6. Fitted to Din Sync's real unit by the whole voice (compare_dinsync.py, SET-A1
* at cutoff 25 to 100 %): tm3 0.35, harmonics 2 to 8 within 0.7 dB on average at three positions, 2.1 dB at 75 %.
* The 12 V rail: IC16 makes it from the 5.333 V reference times 1 + R178 / R179 (2.2k / 1.8k), 11.85 V, not the 12 V
* drawn (D275); with 5 % resistors a unit may sit anywhere from about 11.4 to 12.3 V. vcc sets it.
.param cutoff=0.5 res=1 envmod=0 env=0 acc=0 tm3=0.1642 freq=65.406 sq=0 vcc=11.851 tend=0.2
.param ka=3.47
.param tcut={(exp(ka*cutoff)-1)/(exp(ka)-1)} tenv={(exp(ka*envmod)-1)/(exp(ka)-1)}
.param rcut1={max(50k*tcut, 1)} rcut3={max(50k*(1-tcut), 1)}
.param renv1={max(50k*tenv, 1)} renv3={max(50k*(1-tenv), 1)}
.param rres1={max(50k*res, 1)} rres3={max(50k*(1-res), 1)}
.param rtm3={max(470k*tm3, 1)}

.model QEM NPN(IS=39f XTI=3 EG=1.11 VAF=74.03 BF=416.4 NE=1.259 ISE=6.734f IKF=66.78m XTB=1.5 BR=.7371 NC=2
+ ISC=0 IKR=0 RC=1 CJC=3.638p MJC=.3085 VJC=.75 FC=.5 CJE=4.493p MJE=.2593 VJE=.75 TR=239.5n TF=301.2p ITF=.4
+ VTF=4 XTF=2 RB=10)
.model QPM PNP(IS=39f XTI=3 EG=1.11 VAF=18.7 BF=300 NE=1.5 ISE=0 IKF=80m XTB=1.5 BR=4.977 NC=2 ISC=0 IKR=0
+ RC=2.5 CJC=9.728p MJC=.5776 VJC=.75 FC=.5 CJE=8.063p MJE=.3677 VJE=.75 TR=33.42n TF=179.3p ITF=.4 VTF=4 XTF=6
+ RB=10)
.model QDUAL NPN(IS=10f BF=500 BR=4 VAF=100 CJE=5p CJC=2.5p TF=400p)
.model DEM D(IS=2.52n N=1.752 RS=0.568 CJO=2p)

VCC vcc 0 {vcc}
VR vr 0 5.333
R95 vcc vf 100
C28 vf 0 47u

* The input: the VCO's saw (5.6 to 11.1 V, falling, as vco.cir's) or its square, at its mean for the operating point.
BIN nin 0 V = {freq} <= 0 ? 8.35 : (time < 1u ? 8.35 : ({sq} > 0.5 ? (time*{freq} - floor(time*{freq}) < 0.5 ? 8.8 : 5.333) : 11.1 - 5.5*(time*{freq} - floor(time*{freq}))))
R62 nin n17 220k
C17 n17 nb12l 1u

* Q12's bases: R70 and R98 (2.2k) to C16, held at 5.333 V by R68 (2.2k).
R68 vr n16 2.2k
C16 n16 0 10u
R70 nb12l n16 2.2k
R98 nb12r n16 2.2k

* The ladder.
Q12L nl1 nb12l ne12 QDUAL
Q12R nr1 nb12r ne12 QDUAL
Q13 nl2 nl2 nl1 QEM
Q14 nl3 nl3 nl2 QEM
Q16 nl4 nl4 nl3 QEM
Q15 nr2 nr2 nr1 QEM
Q17 nr3 nr3 nr2 QEM
Q23 nr4 nr4 nr3 QEM
C18 nl1 nr1 0.018u
C19 nl2 nr2 0.033u
C24 nl3 nr3 0.033u
C26 nl4 nr4 0.033u
Q22L vf nb22 nl4 QDUAL
Q22R vf nb22 nr4 QDUAL
R115 vf nb22 10k
C30 nb22 0 10u

* The read-out: Q21 through C27 (right side's top) and C25 (left side's top), biased from 5.333 V through R116 and
* C29, R113 and R114 (100k); its tail Q20 (R116, R112, R109 divide 5.333 V in three; R108 2.2k); R111 and R110 (22k)
* its loads;
* Q19, a follower over R96 (10k), into C14.
R116 vr nbias 10k
C29 nbias 0 1u
C27 nr4 nb21l 0.1u
C25 nl4 nb21r 0.1u
R113 nb21l nbias 100k
R114 nb21r nbias 100k
Q21L nc21l nb21l ne21 QDUAL
Q21R nc21r nb21r ne21 QDUAL
R111 vf nc21l 22k
R110 vf nc21r 22k
R112 nbias nb20 10k
R109 nb20 0 10k
Q20 ne21 nb20 ne20 QEM
R108 ne20 0 2.2k
Q19 vf nc21r ntp6 QEM
R96 ntp6 0 10k
C14 ntp6 nvcf 1u

* C14's loads: RESONANCE's first gang (pin 3 at TP6, pin 1 to ground), and the VCA's input until vca.cir.
RRES3 nvcf nresw {rres3}
RRES1 nresw 0 {rres1}
R121 nvcf n21 220k
C21 n21 vr 0.01u

* The feedback: the wiper through C15 and R67 (2.2k) into Q18's base, held by R99 (100k) at C22's 5.333 V (R66);
* Q18's emitter over R94 (10k) through C23 and R97 (10k) into Q12's right base.
C15 nresw n15 1u
R67 n15 nb18 2.2k
R66 vr n22 100k
C22 n22 0 1u
R99 n22 nb18 100k
Q18 vcc nb18 ne18 QEM
R94 ne18 0 10k
C23 ne18 n23 1u
R97 n23 nb12r 10k

* The current: Q12's emitters through R69 to Q11; Q9's follower at VQ9 (R65, R64 halve 5.333 V).
R69 ne12 nc11 2.2k
Q11 nc11 nb11 nvq9 QEM
R65 vr nb9 10k
R64 nb9 0 10k
Q9 0 nb9 nvq9 QPM
Q10 0 nb10 nb11 QPM
RCUT3 vcc ncutw {rcut3}
RCUT1 ncutw ncut1 {rcut1}
R47 ncut1 nvq9 10k
R73 ncutw ntm3 100k
RTM3 ntm3 nb11 {rtm3}
R71 nb10 nvq9 2.2k

* ENV MOD: the envelope at pin 3, R61 (10k) to VQ9 at pin 1, the wiper through R63 (220k) into Q10's base.
VENV nenv 0 {env}
RENV3 nenv nenvw {renv3}
RENV1 nenvw n61 {renv1}
R61 n61 nvq9 10k
R63 nenvw nb10 220k

* The accent's sweep: D24 from the ACCENT wiper, R46 (47k), RESONANCE's second gang (pin 1 at R46, pin 3 at C13,
* its wiper turning with the first gang) and C13; the wiper through R72 (100k) into Q10's base.
VACC nacc 0 {acc}
D24 nacc nd24 DEM
R46 nd24 nres1b 47k
RRESB1 nres1b nresbw {rres1}
RRESB3 nresbw n13 {rres3}
C13 n13 0 1u
R72 nresbw nb10 100k

.options method=trap reltol=1e-5 abstol=1e-12 vntol=1e-7
.tran 0.5u {tend} 0 0.5u
.end
